        "original_id": "de8303da-0c68-527f-8e39-f3291abf6900",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Pete Townshend, Franc Roddam\n- Bands: The Who\n- Songs: \"5:15\"\n- Works: \"Quadrophenia\" rock opera, Quadrophenia film, soundtrack album\n- Charts: UK Singles Chart, Billboard Hot 100\n\nFacts:\n- Pete Townshend of The Who wrote the song \"5:15\".\n- The song \"5:15\" was part of The Who's 1973 rock opera \"Quadrophenia\".\n- The song \"5:15\" was released as a single and reached No. 20 on the UK Singles Chart.\n- Quadrophenia is a 1979 British drama film loosely based on The Who's 1973 rock opera \"Quadrophenia\".\n- Franc Roddam directed the 1979 film Quadrophenia in his feature directing debut.\n- The 1979 re-release of \"5:15,\" accompanying the film Quadrophenia and its soundtrack album, reached No. 45 on the Billboard Hot 100.",
